{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures","id":115031,"title":"Uratha Cultures","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-17T16:43:43-07:00","id":115031,"title":"Uratha Cultures","content":"Hey all,<br /> <br /> For a while I've been thinking about how the Uratha in the United States seems to have a strong focus on Native American cultural aspects. It has made me wonder who on these forums, who play/storytell Forsaken outside of the United States, have come up with their own variants on Forsaken society which are more suited to the region or country of their setting (beyond taking the snippets of foreign culture found in some Forsaken supplements, such as the Lodge of the Firestick in Australia).<br /> <br /> The Architect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/220-thearchitect","name":"TheArchitect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T00:18:17-07:00","id":115150,"title":"","content":"I'm setting my game in Sweden and and I personally put more empathize on family and the importance of kin, and I'm thinking of generally throwing in more of a Norse kind of stuff. But for the most part I tend to let things go pretty much as they go in the core.<br /> <br /> It isn't radically different but I would think that my style goes more of Uratha as heroic warriors in the Germanic/Norse style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T02:05:20-07:00","id":115175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheArchitect</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, will many Forsaken in your game call themselves Ulfhednar? It strikes me as being a name that the Norse-themed Forsaken might find appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Untill now, none. After this; all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T06:13:30-07:00","id":115245,"title":"","content":"I have set various games in the Australia Outback; I create games with an emphasis on the sheer isolation of the Australia Outback, some pack claim territory larger then countries (it\u2019s actual control on the other hand is very low), and most packs of Uratha claim territory far larger than the rest of the world. Pack is far more important than tribe, it\u2019s not that they don\u2019t they don\u2019t find tribal identification important, it\u2019s that Outback Uratha are clannish and frankly a little xenophobic. The most defining characteristic, however, is that the isolation allows the Uratha to be far more open about themselves, they've no need to hide from the herd, it largely doesn't exist in the outback. Without any need to hide, the conflict between Pure vs Forsaken is far volatile then elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Ignore everything you read about Australia, and Indigenous Australians, in the Lodge of the Firestick. It's depiction of Indigenous Australians is not only inaccurate, it's also incredibly offensive. I believe the author mistaken what is an incredibly offensive ethnic slur; it\u2019s like calling someone the N-word, for what they thought was a generic term for white people. Sadly, White Wolf has never been very successful at depicting Australia in print.<br /> <br /> edit: I come off far more harsh then I intend to be, okay, they're not even close to accurate and came off as a little offensive; but at least they're not ignoring us, like we don't even exist or only deserving a couple of sentences. We're a continent, we exist, would it kill ya to put more Australian stuff in the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1072-theye1","user":"theye1","date":". 04-18-2014, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1072-theye1","name":"theye1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1072_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T06:40:43-07:00","id":115252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theye1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures?p=115245#post115245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;snip&gt; Sadly, White Wolf has never been very successful at depicting Australia in print.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm working to correct this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theye1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures?p=115245#post115245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">edit: I come off far more harsh then I intend to be, okay, they're not even close to accurate and came off as a little offensive; but at least they're not ignoring us, like we don't even exist or only deserving a couple of sentences. We're a continent, we exist, would it kill ya to put more Australian stuff in the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Working on this too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T07:48:58-07:00","id":115269,"title":"","content":"This is something that White Wolf has traditionally not been that great at... and which the recent Chronicles stuff is doing a very good job of correcting. Blood &amp; Smoke has some very nice 'alternate culture vampires', and looks like Idigam will do the same for Werewolves. Including Australian werewolves, it would appear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T08:12:15-07:00","id":115287,"title":"","content":"The Rage had an early guide to different continents and specific countries. Then you have the examples in Shadows of the UK and finally, there's a bunch of different cultural flavors for the Uratha displayed in Lodges: the Splintered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T10:03:34-07:00","id":115350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures?p=115287#post115287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rage had an early guide to different continents and specific countries. Then you have the examples in Shadows of the UK and finally, there's a bunch of different cultural flavors for the Uratha displayed in Lodges: the Splintered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Splintered is where Lodge of the Firestick is from. The Lodge of the Hungry Ghosts, neat though it is, has some egregious use of <i>gairaigo</i> that really doesn't make sense - the Japanese language <i>has</i> words for &quot;skin&quot; and &quot;bronze&quot; that don't sound as awkward as <i>sukin</i> and <i>buronzu</i>, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T16:52:37-07:00","id":115600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures?p=115252#post115252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm working to correct this.<br /> <br /> Working on this too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay! Little advice, though, try to avoid the cliches about Indigenous Australians being more 'mystical' or more in 'tune' with the land.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1072-theye1","name":"theye1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1072_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T19:09:55-07:00","id":115642,"title":"","content":"'Magical native culture' is something Stew strongly wants us to avoid, so no worries there.<br /> <br /> (Plus that isn't something I would write unless there was a good reason - one specific family group in a specific area, maybe, if the story needed it. Blanket mysticism - no thank you.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T03:27:48-07:00","id":116430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheArchitect</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, will many Forsaken in your game call themselves Ulfhednar? It strikes me as being a name that the Norse-themed Forsaken might find appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods above... That's genius!<br /> Hmm. What to call the Bale Hounds and the Pure. Hmm.<br /> <br /> Previously I've just used the First Tongue names for the factions, Tribes et cetera.<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly though, Werewolf packs are very close to the old Norse ideas of family. It helped if you were born into it, sure, but there was nothing wrong with adoption. And adopted brother was your brother for all intents and purposes.<br /> <br /> The big problem I had with Scandinavian games is that a lot of the folklore is more fey than spiritual. Playing a traditionally Norse game is a lot easier if you do Changeling than if you do Werewolf.<br /> Then, on the other hand, the anthromorphization of the spirit world for the last fifteen hundred years or so might've had SOME effect on the spirit world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T04:48:39-07:00","id":116444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheArchitect</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures#post115031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey all, For a while I've been thinking about how the Uratha in the United States seems to have a strong focus on Native American cultural aspects. It has made me wonder who on these forums, who play/storytell Forsaken outside of the United States, have come up with their own variants on Forsaken society which are more suited to the region or country of their setting (beyond taking the snippets of foreign culture found in some Forsaken supplements, such as the Lodge of the Firestick in Australia). The Architect</div> </div> </div> </div> It's based on Tribal and animism themes, which is hardly limited to the indigenous population of the Americas. It's simple enough to evoke a tribal / clannish attitude in any country, and animism is an easy enough religion to adapt anywhere. Take, say, japan. Werewolf is at home with the dominant Shinto religion, and the culture lends itself to association with familial clan types. Tribes are easily philosophies. What more could you ask for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T06:40:32-07:00","id":116476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheArchitect</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Balehounds: Surturi, because they're trying to corrupt everything, which can bring around the collapse of society - collapse enough societies and you might end up with a nuclear war... Ragnarok, to a degree.<br /> <br /> Pure Tribes: vargr seems likely. The vargr are connected to Fenrir, who the Pure could logically believe is Father Wolf depending on how you present the mythology of norse Forsaken. Especially if they see one of the five firstborn who killed him as an embodiment of Vioarr.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The problem with calling the Pure Vargr is that varg is the common Swedish name for wolf.<br /> <br /> Father Wolf as Fenris is probably more of a cultish view of it all, after all, there is one big, destructive Firstborn calling himself Fenris, and I don't think many go against the word of Destroyer Wolf. And since he lives, Ragnar\u00f6k hasn't come yet, although I think both the Predator Kings and the Bale Hounds work for it, although in differing ways. The Predator Kings want to bring about the Fimbulwinter, where during several years of winter, legions of wolves will come out of the woods and tear down civilization. That sounds a lot like the Predator King dream.<br /> <br /> Bale Hounds are just all for apocalypse in general. That means they have, after all, won. Surturgarmar. Surt's dogs. Yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T11:58:31-07:00","id":118033,"title":"","content":"I agree that Vargr is far to close to the word &quot;varg&quot;.<br /> <br /> The idea that the Predator Kings wants to have a Fimbult Winter to tear down civilization sounds gold to me. I also lik the word of Suturgarmar very much, I'll steal all of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T16:00:34-07:00","id":120594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures?p=118033#post118033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that Vargr is far to close to the word &quot;varg&quot;.<br /> <br /> The idea that the Predator Kings wants to have a Fimbult Winter to tear down civilization sounds gold to me. I also lik the word of Suturgarmar very much, I'll steal all of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably the greatest honour one can get on a forum like these. Thanks. Seriously. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By the way, are you Swedish? If so, do you have any decent names for the Tribes? Because, with the exception of the Storm Lords, all of them sound excessively dorky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T03:29:17-07:00","id":120867,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to peoples' reaction to the spread of Hunting Grounds we're depicting in IC!<br /> <br /> I will say that it <i>is</i> a challenge to fit everything you want into the word count for a Hunting Ground and inevitably certain elements of a location or culture that you'd love to cover has to be left by the wayside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T04:50:45-07:00","id":120882,"title":"","content":"Full agreement with that. Hard to keep the word count down, and I reckon I could fill a book with Hunting Grounds from around the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T09:24:41-07:00","id":120976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures?p=120882#post120882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Full agreement with that. Hard to keep the word count down, and I reckon I could fill a book with Hunting Grounds from around the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunting Grounds: Brazil anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T10:29:13-07:00","id":121016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures?p=120594#post120594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's probably the greatest honour one can get on a forum like these. Thanks. Seriously. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By the way, are you Swedish? If so, do you have any decent names for the Tribes? Because, with the exception of the Storm Lords, all of them sound excessively dorky.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're welcome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And I am indeed Swedish. I'll think a little about names for Tribes an come back with some suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T06:58:03-07:00","id":121680,"title":"","content":"After pitching the two Hunting Grounds that I am contributing to IC, I was immediately struck by inspiration for another three I'd like to do as well.<br /> <br /> There's really a wealth of options for unique and interesting Hunting Grounds. Once we've gotten IC sorted, might see if Stew'd be interested in putting up any more sample Hunting Grounds in his dev blogs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T07:32:29-07:00","id":121688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures?p=121680#post121680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After pitching the two Hunting Grounds that I am contributing to IC, I was immediately struck by inspiration for another three I'd like to do as well.<br /> <br /> There's really a wealth of options for unique and interesting Hunting Grounds. Once we've gotten IC sorted, might see if Stew'd be interested in putting up any more sample Hunting Grounds in his dev blogs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you throw out what Hunting Grounds DIDN'T get in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:51:42-07:00","id":121800,"title":"","content":"@Seidmadr: Wouldn't that list be colossal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:59:48-07:00","id":121809,"title":"","content":"Sorry - it's up to Stew what gets teased about the Hunting Grounds and when, if they get revealed at all before the book's release <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T11:17:33-07:00","id":121869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures?p=120594#post120594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's probably the greatest honour one can get on a forum like these. Thanks. Seriously. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By the way, are you Swedish? If so, do you have any decent names for the Tribes? Because, with the exception of the Storm Lords, all of them sound excessively dorky.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, what do you think of these very loose translation?<br /> <br /> <br /> Blood Talons - R\u00f6dklor<br /> Bone Shadows - no idea<br /> Hunters in Darkness - Skuggj\u00e4gare<br /> Storm Lords - Stormfurstar<br /> Iron Masters - J\u00e4rnm\u00e4stare<br /> <br /> Predator Kings - Rovkungar<br /> Fire-Touched - Eldvigda<br /> Ivory Claws - no idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T22:09:57-07:00","id":122194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures?p=121869#post121869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood Talons - R\u00f6dklor<br /> Bone Shadows - no idea<br /> Hunters in Darkness - Skuggj\u00e4gare<br /> Storm Lords - Stormfurstar<br /> Iron Masters - J\u00e4rnm\u00e4stare<br /> <br /> Predator Kings - Rovkungar<br /> Fire-Touched - Eldvigda<br /> Ivory Claws - no idea</div> </div> </div> </div>They look cool, but I'm not Sweaden - myabe you could wrote also phonetic variatnas also for Enlish speakers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T05:15:19-07:00","id":123075,"title":"","content":"I'd love to but I'm afraid I'm not very skilled with phonetics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T09:16:49-07:00","id":123207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures?p=122194#post122194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They look cool, but I'm not Sweaden - myabe you could wrote also phonetic variatnas also for Enlish speakers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Google Translate has a pronunciation button. It is not perfect, but it is better than nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T11:37:13-07:00","id":123900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures?p=121869#post121869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ok, what do you think of these very loose translation?<br /> <br /> <br /> Blood Talons - R\u00f6dklor<br /> Bone Shadows - no idea<br /> Hunters in Darkness - Skuggj\u00e4gare<br /> Storm Lords - Stormfurstar<br /> Iron Masters - J\u00e4rnm\u00e4stare<br /> <br /> Predator Kings - Rovkungar<br /> Fire-Touched - Eldvigda<br /> Ivory Claws - no idea</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty neat! I thought Stormherrar was better though, lords rather than princes, after all.<br /> Ivory Claws is really hard to translate, could go for a variant of the blood talons' name? Vitklor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T11:33:33-07:00","id":124635,"title":"","content":"Don't really like the idea of Stormherrar since &quot;herr&quot; och &quot;herre&quot; kind of feels like 19th century and early 20th century urban middle class to me. Just like the word &quot;herrskap&quot;. &quot;Furste&quot; feels more archaic, heavy and traditional in a way that I think that the tribes should feel.<br /> <br /> I regards to the Ivory Claws I agree tha &quot;vitklor&quot; could work for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T19:12:54-07:00","id":124913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures?p=124635#post124635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't really like the idea of Stormherrar since &quot;herr&quot; och &quot;herre&quot; kind of feels like 19th century and early 20th century urban middle class to me. Just like the word &quot;herrskap&quot;. &quot;Furste&quot; feels more archaic, heavy and traditional in a way that I think that the tribes should feel.<br /> <br /> I regards to the Ivory Claws I agree tha &quot;vitklor&quot; could work for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Valid point. Also, when I look at it again, I can't unsee the similarity between Stormherre and Domherre. Which is kind of demeaning.<br /> <br /> De \u00d6vergivna is an obvious name for the Forsaken. It doesn't just work well as a direct translation, but is also a nice in-joke. I'm tempted to bring it all the way up to De \u00d6vergivnas Arm\u00e9.<br /> <br /> The Pure is a bit worse. De Rena, or possibly Renade is kinda weak. Or what do you say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T04:14:02-07:00","id":125110,"title":"","content":"True about the Pure and I love the pun with &quot;De \u00d6vergivna.&quot; taking it all the way to &quot;De \u00d6vergivnas Arm\u00e9&quot; would however be a bit to much.<br /> <br /> In regards to what word we could call the Pure I'm not so sure either. &quot;De Rena&quot; could work but I don't think that it carries the real meaning with it that i should give. How about &quot;de Skuldl\u00f6sa&quot; or &quot;Rengivna&quot;? The more I think the less I can come up with. Maybe it would just be best to make it &quot;de Rena&quot; straight off?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T23:04:46-07:00","id":136329,"title":"","content":"From what I see, in Scandinavia, we will have <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M%C3%A1ni\" target=\"_blank\">Father Moon</a> and Mother Wolf. as avatars of those primal beings. With Fenris being the Firstborn, he can't be also the Father Wolf himself. Very good candidate for Mother Wolf is mother of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hati_Hr%C3%B3%C3%B0vitnisson\" target=\"_blank\">M\u00e1nagarmr</a>, that himself looked as one of Firstborns. Interesting would be interpretation that Father Moon was seduced by Mother Wolf and raped by her to make Uratha, wouldn't you think? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-14-2014, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T07:17:41-07:00","id":136652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures?p=116430#post116430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gods above... That's genius!<br /> Hmm. What to call the Bale Hounds and the Pure. Hmm.<br /> <br /> Previously I've just used the First Tongue names for the factions, Tribes et cetera.<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly though, Werewolf packs are very close to the old Norse ideas of family. It helped if you were born into it, sure, but there was nothing wrong with adoption. And adopted brother was your brother for all intents and purposes.<br /> <br /> The big problem I had with Scandinavian games is that a lot of the folklore is more fey than spiritual. Playing a traditionally Norse game is a lot easier if you do Changeling than if you do Werewolf.<br /> Then, on the other hand, the anthromorphization of the spirit world for the last fifteen hundred years or so might've had SOME effect on the spirit world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe you could call the Bale Hounds &quot;Dingos&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> Please don't shoot me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Personally, I think a werewolf game would be most effective in places of the world which are largely devoid of a monotheistic religion. Many of the ancient cultures worshiped totems or animals and spirits, but they were wiped out by the presence of the various divisions of Christian sects. If you focus more on places in the world that still adhere to these old customs, Werewolves could fit much better. Sure, you have Indian Reservations in America as the most obvious choice, but look at other places in the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> Scouting out the dominant religions in a particular territory should give a general idea of how spiritual the people are, as well as how likely they are to have shapeshifters roaming the countryside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-14-2014, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:19:01-07:00","id":136795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures?p=136652#post136652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Personally, I think a werewolf game would be most effective in places of the world which are largely devoid of a monotheistic religion. Many of the ancient cultures worshiped totems or animals and spirits, but they were wiped out by the presence of the various divisions of Christian sects. If you focus more on places in the world that still adhere to these old customs, Werewolves could fit much better. Sure, you have Indian Reservations in America as the most obvious choice, but look at other places in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Modern Scandinavia have very much resurface of neo-paganism. People are literally going back to the religion of they forefathers. The problem is with Norse myths, everything is on opposite from <b>Werewolf</b> corebook - Mother Luna should be Father Moon, probably Father Wolf should be made in to Mother Wolf and I'm not sure that connotation of Fenris with Forsaken Tribes don't mean they want to make literal Ragnar\u00f6k to the Pure.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:24:53-07:00","id":136799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures?p=136795#post136795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Modern Scandinavia have very much resurface of neo-paganism. People are literally going back to the religion of they forefathers. The problem is with Norse myths, everything is on opposite from <b>Werewolf</b> corebook - Mother Luna should be Father Moon, probably Father Wolf should be made in to Mother Wolf and I'm not sure that connotation of Fenris with Forsaken Tribes don't mean they want to make literal Ragnar\u00f6k to the Pure.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Rule 63 Werewolf the Forsaken?<br /> <br /> <br /> That actually sounds pretty fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:50:28-07:00","id":136821,"title":"","content":"First to remember - I'm Polish, just interested in Norse and Slavic myths, but my knowledge is mostly from Internet. If you have better ideas and/or sources, point this a way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Now I found nowhere proper myth, but this interesting story for building Scandinavian <b>Forsaken</b> myths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenris Shrine</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the Great Wolf, Fenris, began to run amuck, he first went back to the place where he was born. Tyr and the other Aesir had tried to keep him from going back to the Iron Wood, but one day he escaped and fled to his birthplace, and was reunited with his mother Angrboda, and his werewolf half-siblings. It is not known what happened to him there, save that when he left, his maddened devouring rage had begun in earnest, and a wolf-woman of the Jarnvidur had borne two wolf-pups, the very image of their father. In another account, the mother of Hati and Skoll was Angrboda herself, by Fenris her son, but we may never know the truth of this. Skoll's name means &quot;treachery&quot; in Old Norse, while Hati's name means &quot;Hater&quot;. Hati is also sometimes given two different last names - Hr\u00f3\u00f0vitnisson (Son of Rage) and Managarm (Moon-hound).</div> </div> </div> </div>Source: <a href=\"http://www.northernpaganism.org/shrines/fenrir/writing/the-sons-of-fenrir-hati-and-skoll.html\" target=\"_blank\">Fenris Shrine</a><br /> <br /> The part of &quot;he escaped and fled to his birthplace, and was reunited with his mother Angrboda, and his werewolf half-siblings&quot; would mean that acording to this myth Fenris were a half-sibling with werewolves and they all would be children of Angrboda. Could it be she was Wolf Mother that seduced Mani, Moon Father?<br /> <br /> More we go in to reaserch, more Angrboda looks like Scandinavian Mother Luna...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angerboda</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">N<span style=\"font-size:13px\">ot only is Angerboda\u2019s identity unclear, but She is also virtually impossible to classify; She may be a giantess, a troll-queen, a member of the Vanir pantheon, or some or all of the above. She may be old Loki\u2019s twin sister. She may be something so old She defies definition. She is a shape-shifter, which accounts for some of this confusion. </span> Angerboda is a Goddess of death and destruction as well as birth and life. She is Freya\u2019s personal messenger.<br /> (,,,)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Gullveig means \u201cpower of gold\u201d and She may be Angerboda\u2019s alter ego. She may also be known as Heid, the \u201cshining\u201d or \u201cgleaming\u201d one. Gullveig asks the Aesir for a gift of gold for the Vanir into whose territory they have moved. The Aesir call Her a witch and condemn Her to death. Thor seizes and binds Her, and She is pierced with spears like a pig on a spit and roasted on a pyre. She burns, Her ashes are scattered, and yet miraculously She reappears, alive and good as new. The Aesir recapture Her and repeat their actions. Gullveig is burned and resurrected three times.</span><br /> Angerboda returned to life in Valhalla twice, but the third time She found Herself in Her home, the Iron Wood. She never re-enters Asgard because the Aesir long to destroy Her.<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> Angerboda\u2019s children include Hel, Queen of Death, the Midguard Serpent, the Fenris Wolf, and the wolves responsible for solar and lunar eclipses. Other sons are identified as werewolves. She is the grandmother of Trolls.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Source: </span><a href=\"http://www.sacredhaven.ca/angerboda\" target=\"_blank\">Angerboda</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">It looks like she would have a thing with Father Moon in past, only now is really pissed off on her ex. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: I've made Scandinavian Forsaken creation myth - he is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths\">this topic</a>. I took the names from your transaltions. Hopes you like it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-15-2014, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}